[groq-gpt-oss] evals/prompts/lib/skill-p:
Below is a **complete, copy‑and‑paste ready** example that

1. **Loads every SVG icon** that lives on your own domain (`/icons/<category>.svg`).  
2. **Registers each icon with MapLibre** under a name that matches the `category` property in your GeoJSON.  
3. **Adds the 5 000‑point GeoJSON source**.  
4. **Draws a symbol layer** that uses the matching icon, lets the icons shrink when you zoom out, and **prevents them from piling on top of each other** (they disappear when they would collide).

> **MapLibre GL JS version 6** (the API is the same as v2.x of Mapbox GL JS, so the code works for both).

---

## 1️⃣  HTML skeleton

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>MapLibre – 40 category icons + 5 000 venues</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

  <!-- MapLibre GL JS v6 (CDN) -->
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>

  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; padding:0; height:100%; }
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script>
/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   CONFIGURATION
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
const MAPBOX_STYLE = 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json'; // any style you like
const CENTER = [ -73.985130, 40.758896 ]; // example: Times Square
const ZOOM   = 12;

// 1️⃣  List of all category ids (the same strings that appear in the
//     `category` property of each venue).  Keep them in the same order
//     as the SVG files on your server.
const CATEGORIES = [
  'restaurant', 'cafe', 'bar', 'museum', 'park',
  'hotel', 'store', 'theatre', 'library', 'gym',
  // … add the rest (total ≈ 40) …
];

// Base URL where the SVG files live.  The code will request
//   `${ICON_BASE_URL}/${category}.svg`
const ICON_BASE_URL = 'https://your‑domain.com/icons';

/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   MAP INITIALISATION
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: MAPBOX_STYLE,
  center: CENTER,
  zoom: ZOOM,
  // optional – improves performance on low‑end devices
  preserveDrawingBuffer: false,
  antialias: true
});

/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   2️⃣  Load all SVG icons and register them with the map
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
function loadSvgIcon(category) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const url = `${ICON_BASE_URL}/${category}.svg`;
    // `Image` works for SVG as long as the server sends the correct MIME type.
    const img = new Image();
    img.crossOrigin = 'anonymous';          // needed if the domain is different
    img.onload = () => {
      // MapLibre can use the HTMLImageElement directly.
      // `sdf: true` lets you recolor the icon with `icon-color` later (optional).
      map.addImage(category, img, { sdf: true });
      resolve();
    };
    img.onerror = (e) => reject(`Failed to load ${url}`);
    img.src = url;
  });
}

/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   3️⃣  Load the venue GeoJSON (replace the URL with yours)
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
function loadVenueGeoJSON() {
  return fetch('https://your‑domain.com/data/venues.geojson')
    .then(r => {
      if (!r.ok) throw new Error('GeoJSON fetch failed');
      return r.json();
    });
}

/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   4️⃣  When the map is ready, load icons → source → layer
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */
map.once('load', async () => {
  try {
    // ---- 4a. Load every icon (Promise.all resolves when *all* are ready) ----
    await Promise.all(CATEGORIES.map(cat => loadSvgIcon(cat)));
    console.log('✅ All icons loaded');

    // ---- 4b. Add the GeoJSON source ----
    const venues = await loadVenueGeoJSON();
    map.addSource('venues', {
      type: 'geojson',
      data: venues,
      // optional clustering if you ever want it (kept off for now)
      // cluster: true,
      // clusterRadius: 50
    });

    // ---- 4c. Add the symbol layer that uses the icons ----
    map.addLayer({
      id: 'venue-icons',
      type: 'symbol',
      source: 'venues',
      layout: {
        // The icon name is taken directly from the feature's `category` property.
        // If a feature has a category that wasn't loaded, the icon will be invisible.
        'icon-image': ['get', 'category'],

        // Scale the icons with zoom – feel free to tweak the numbers.
        'icon-size': [
          'interpolate',
          ['linear'],
          ['zoom'],
          10, 0.5,   // at zoom 10 → 50 % of original size
          15, 1.0,   // at zoom 15 → 100 % of original size
          18, 1.5    // at zoom 18 → 150 % of original size
        ],

        // Do **not** allow icons to overlap.  When two would collide,
        // the lower‑priority one (the one added later in the source) is hidden.
        'icon-allow-overlap': false,

        // If an icon would overlap another, simply hide it (instead of
        // pushing the other one away).  This keeps the map readable.
        'icon-optional': true,

        // Optional: keep the icons upright when the map is rotated.
        'icon-rotate': 0,
        'icon-pitch-alignment': 'map',
        'icon-rotation-alignment': 'map'
      },
      paint: {
        // Optional: recolor all icons at once (works because we set `sdf:true` above)
        // 'icon-color': '#ff6600',
        // Optional: add a subtle halo so icons stand out on any basemap
        'icon-halo-color': '#ffffff',
        'icon-halo-width': 1,
        'icon-halo-blur': 0.5
      }
    });

    console.log('✅ Layer added – you should now see the venues');
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('❌ Something went wrong:', err);
  }
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## How it works, step‑by‑step

| Step | What happens | Why it matters |
|------|--------------|----------------|
| **1️⃣  List of categories** | `CATEGORIES` is an array of the exact strings that appear in each feature’s `category` property. | The name you give an icon to MapLibre **must match** the property value you later reference (`icon-image: ['get','category']`). |
| **2️⃣  Load SVG icons** | For each category we create an `Image`, set its `src` to `…/icons/<category>.svg`, wait for `onload`, then call `map.addImage(category, img, {sdf:true})`. | `addImage` registers the SVG so it can be used in a style. `sdf:true` makes the icon “signed‑distance‑field” capable of being recolored with `icon-color` (optional but handy). |
| **3️⃣  Load the GeoJSON** | A simple `fetch` → `response.json()` gives us the 5 000 venue features. | Keeping the source separate from the icons lets you swap data without re‑loading the icons. |
| **4️⃣  Symbol layer** | `icon-image` is data‑driven (`['get','category']`). `icon-allow-overlap:false` + `icon-optional:true` tells the renderer to **hide** an icon when it would collide with another, instead of stacking them. `icon-size` is interpolated with zoom so the symbols shrink when you zoom out. | This satisfies the requirement *“zoomed out the icons shouldn't pile up on top of each other.”* |
| **Optional tweaks** | * `icon-color` / `icon-halo-*` for better contrast.<br>* `cluster:true` if you later decide you want clustering for very low zoom levels. | You can adapt the visual style without touching the data‑driven part. |

---

### 🎯  What you need to change for your own project

| Placeholder | What to replace |
|-------------|-----------------|
| `https://your-domain.com/icons` | Base URL where the 40 + SVG files live. |
| `CATEGORIES` array | Exact list of category identifiers (file names without the `.svg` extension). |
| `https://your-domain.com/data/venues.geojson` | URL (or inline object) of your 5 000‑point GeoJSON. |
| `MAPBOX_STYLE` | Any MapLibre style URL you prefer (or a custom style JSON). |
| `CENTER` & `ZOOM` | Initial view for your area of interest. |

